==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Gladios the Annihilator''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''God-Emperor Gladios''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Gladios, like most other Dragon Emperors Ubers, has high cost, health and damage, as well as slow movement speed and attack animation. Gladios has the interesting niche of knocking back and slowing Traitless enemies, which, combined with his durability, makes him effective against [[Master A.]] or [[Dolphina]]. However, some Traitless enemies such as [[Henry]], [[Croakley]] or [[Mr. Mole]] are able to keep him at bay making it so he can almost never attack. His attack rate is not low enough to handle more difficult situations as in [[Procrastinator Parade]] or [[Cloned Farmers]] without serious support from units such as [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]] and Research [[Cat Combo]] supported [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]], so do not use him unless the spam of [[R.Ost]]s is manageable, as in [[Heaven's Oasis]], [[Beverly Hills Scoop]] and [[Fainting Porch]].

Still, due to the lack of competition, he still manages to be a very valuable [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless unit]] and can prove very useful in most Traitless-centered stages, most notably the [[:Category:Crazed Cat Stages|Crazed/Maniac stages]] and [[No Return Flights]]. As a generalist, his high health allows him to stay on the field for a while and deal worthwhile damage, but speed and cost bring him down, so don't use him outside of his niche unless being slow isn't too big of an issue in a stage.

==='''True Form'''===
The improved health is nice, but the guaranteed knockback and slow are what make this worth the [[Catfruit]]. Nothing else changes, and neither does Gladios' usage. He's either the occasional slower generalist, or a monster to any Traitless enemy he is effective on.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Mini-Wave''' is inconsistent due to its 50% activation chance when maxed and Gladios' long attack cycle, but it does serve to extend his CC effects when it occurs, reaching up to 732.5 range away from him and impeding any traitless target vulnerable to Waves. '''Survives''' is a nice bonus, but is unlikely to come into play, considering he outranges a decent amount of Traitless enemies, and has a gargantuan health stat. '''Cost Down''' is unlikely to be worth the NP, as while it does bring his cost under 5,000¢, spending 175 NP for that alone is not really worth it. As typical, he also receives stat talents, and thanks to Gladios's decent generalist stats these can actually be useful, though as always if you want to improve his generalist usage, invest your Catseyes before your NP.

